    <bpmn:process id="W_W3262" name="W3262. Litigation Hold Initiation &amp; Evidence Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Reasonable anticipation of litigation (W3257); regulatory investigation
Frequency: Per matter
Volume: ~20–40 active holds
Owner: Litigation Counsel
Participants: Litigation Counsel, Legal Ops Mgr, Records (links to VS-88), IT (links to VS-27/VS-99), Business Owners, Custodians
Source: workflow W3262 — Litigation Hold Initiation &amp; Evidence Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3262_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3262_Lane1" name="Litigation Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3262_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3262_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3262_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3262_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3262_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3262_Start3" name="Reasonable anticipation of litigation (W3257); regulatory investigation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3262_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3262_Task4" name="Litigation Counsel issue litigation hold notice: identify custodians and data…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Litigation Counsel issue litigation hold notice: identify custodians and data sources (email, files, ERP records, CCTV per VS-23.2, POS/WMS data), suspend retention/deletion for hold scope (executed by VS-88 W2990 legal-hold), notify custodians of preservation obligation and consequences of spoliation
Responsible (R): Litigation Counsel / Legal Ops Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per matter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3262_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3262_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3262_Task5" name="Coordinate evidence collection and preservation: collect and preserve relevant…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Coordinate evidence collection and preservation: collect and preserve relevant documents/data (chain of custody per VS-88 W2990), coordinate IT for electronic evidence (links to VS-27/VS-99), preserve CCTV/physical evidence within retention windows, manage privilege and protective orders
Responsible (R): Litigation Counsel / Records / IT
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per matter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3262_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3262_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3262_Task6" name="Release hold at matter close: when litigation/investigation concludes, issue…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Release hold at matter close: when litigation/investigation concludes, issue hold-release to records (links to VS-88) to resume normal retention/deletion; document hold lifecycle for audit (links to VS-21/VS-22.2)
Responsible (R): Litigation Counsel / Records
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: At close</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3262_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3262_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3262_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3262_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3262_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-529 (ensure controlled execution — Legal Matter, Case &amp; Outside Counsel Management (PA-100.1).) | - operational: timely hold and preservation; operational: scoped holds and custodian discipline
Owner: Litigation Counsel</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
